sentences.l:
Yan Yuan said: “May I ask its items?”
The Master said: “What is not the rites, do not look at;
what is not the rites, do not listen to;
what is not the rites, do not say;
what is not the rites, do not do.”
Yan Yuan said:
“Though I, Hui, am not quick,
let me make this saying my business.”

Zigong said: “A pity!
Your words, sir, are a gentleman's;
but a team of four does not catch the tongue.”

Pattern is as plain stuff;
plain stuff is as pattern.
The stripped hide of a tiger or leopard is as the stripped hide of a dog or sheep.

He said: “Two —
I still do not have enough;
how then could I take the tithe?”

Zizhang asked about government.
The Master said: “Dwell on it without wearying;
carry it out with wholeheartedness.”

The Master said: “The gentleman completes what is fine in others;
he does not complete what is bad in others.
The small man reverses this.”

Now making one's way:
plain and straight, and loving what is right;
examining words and observing faces;
minding how to put himself below others —
in a state he is sure to make his way,
in a house he is sure to make his way.

Zigong asked about friends.
The Master said: “Advise him wholeheartedly and guide him well;
if that will not serve, then stop;
do not let yourself be shamed in it.”
